     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily. I know that's frustrating, and I'm not questioning your authority as the attending. The order is 6,400 mg/day, double the maximum labeled dose. I don't know of any indication where that dose gives more benefit, and the GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular risks rise sharply with it. Ibuprofen's analgesic and anti-inflammatory effect plateaus well below that dose. Because the risk is high and I can't see a benefit that would justify it, I won't place it myself.\n\nHere's what I can do right now:\n- **Enter 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum recommended dose. I can add a note such as \"max dose; reassess need daily.\"\n- **Enter a different regimen** if you tell me the indication, such as 600 mg four times daily, or scheduled ibuprofen with acetaminophen.\n- **Add a GI protection order** such as a PPI, if you want one alongside the NSAID.\n\nIf you still want the higher dose, you would need to enter it directly in the order system. It would then go through pharmacy verification, where a clinical pharmacist can review it with you. I'm glad to help with any of the options above."
      }
     ],
